Debounce delays a function until the caller has stopped triggering it for `wait` ms. It's ideal for search boxes and window resize.

```javascript
function debounce(fn, wait = 300) {
  let timer;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), wait);
  };
}

const onSearch = debounce(q => fetch(`/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`), 400);
input.addEventListener("input", e => onSearch(e.target.value));
```

Its cousin, **throttle**, runs at most once per interval instead of waiting for silence.

